WEBVTT

00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:09.720
From Hollywood, the Jack Benny Program.

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:35.040
thank you very very much ladies and gentlemen and welcome to the show

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:43.420
now tonight for what oh for heaven's sake

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:49.040
i forgot to pull down my pants when i got off my bicycle

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:57.640
oh gee now this is it's not uh it's not really what you think

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:59.740
i don't ride a bicycle to the studio

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.560
just to save on gas, you see.

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:06.290
I just happen to think that it's good exercise, you know.

00:01:06.510 --> 00:01:10.410
Now, you take in Europe, nearly everybody rides a bicycle

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:12.030
and nobody thinks anything of it.

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:16.770
But here, I don't know, everybody stares at me.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:20.920
I guess maybe it's because mine has three wheels.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:28.960
But bicycle riding is really good for you.

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:29.900
It's wonderful exercise.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:37.530
Now, I knew a man in Beverly Hills, 92 years old.

00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:42.390
Imagine, 92 years old, who never went anywhere in a car,

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:43.840
always on a bicycle.

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:47.470
And his legs were so developed that,

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:51.790
well, you won't believe this, but three weeks ago, he died,

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:54.780
and they have to keep postponing the services

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:55.980
until they catch him.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:13.700
Tonight when you drive home, if you happen to see an old man riding a bicycle with his arms folded, he is not showing off.

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:21.810
But getting back to exercise, you know, I don't think that people do enough of it.

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:25.460
They don't take advantage of the, um...

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:29.860
What is this anyway?

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:40.670
Hey, hey, fella, fella, I was right in the middle of my monologue, and you dropped the mic in my face.

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:41.210
I did?

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:43.950
Oh, I'm sorry. I must have dozed off.

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:49.920
Dozed off?

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:52.340
Oh, boy, what a night I had last night.

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:56.270
Well, look, that's not my problem. Now sleep on your own time.

00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:59.970
On my own time? How can I sleep with a kid of mine yelling and screaming at...

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.040
3 o'clock in the morning.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:02.820
I'd walk that kid up and down,

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:03.960
up and down, up and down.

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:06.260
And my wife, my wife, she doesn't hear this.

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:07.180
She's sound asleep.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:09.500
Look, I'm not interested in your wife.

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:10.920
Well, neither am I.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:15.960
But you can't break up a home

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:18.520
just because your wife can wear the same shoes that you do.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:21.660
Look, I don't care.

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:23.780
They're a little tight, but she gets them on.

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:28.020
Look, don't tell me your problems.

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:29.940
I'm not a psychiatrist, I'm a comedian.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.920
Well, you could have fooled me.

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:36.670
Never mind, then.

00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:38.830
Now, cut that out and just tend to your business.

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:39.770
And stay awake.

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:40.430
Okay.

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:43.190
Now, you know, I fell asleep here last week, too.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:46.950
What are you talking about?

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:49.050
You weren't even working here last week.

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:49.750
I know.

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:50.930
I was in the audience.

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:59.790
Now, stop the whole business.

00:03:59.850 --> 00:03:59.970
Just...

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:01.590
Do what you're supposed to do.

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:02.410
Okay, okay.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:04.830
I don't know.

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:07.400
I don't know how I ever get a show on

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:09.100
with all the troubles I go through.

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:12.640
Anyway, I'm not going to let that upset me tonight

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:14.240
because, ladies and gentlemen,

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:16.700
we have a real, real good show for you.

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:18.360
And I'm going to introduce a young lady

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:19.820
I know you'll be very happy to meet.

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:23.800
She's from Japan, only been in this country a short time.

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:27.850
And she's already starred in the international company

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:29.290
of Flower Drum Song.

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:32.120
And she's very, very cute and very talented.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:33.860
And right now she's going to sing a song for us.

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:36.900
So here she is, Miss Romy Yamada.

00:06:37.390 --> 00:06:38.810
Romy, come out here, would you please?

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:46.300
I want to tell you that you sang that song just beautifully.

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:47.060
Thank you.

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:52.250
You know, it must be exciting being in the United States for the first time.

00:06:52.530 --> 00:06:54.150
Oh, yes, very exciting.

00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:57.970
Especially now that I'm making my first appearance on television.

00:06:58.390 --> 00:06:59.970
Yeah, this is your first appearance, and I'm...

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:02.340
I'm thrilled about it, too, being on my show.

00:07:02.540 --> 00:07:05.740
Well, tell me, are you enjoying your visit

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:06.460
here in Los Angeles?

00:07:06.740 --> 00:07:09.540
Yes, very much, meeting nice people

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:12.180
and seeing many interesting places of city.

00:07:12.420 --> 00:07:14.620
And had especially good time yesterday

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:15.680
when at your house.

00:07:16.820 --> 00:07:17.820
At my house yesterday?

00:07:18.520 --> 00:07:19.600
You were at my house when?

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:21.060
At noontime.

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:23.900
You were at my house at noon?

00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:27.080
Yes, that is where sightseeing bus stop

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:28.880
to let passengers buy lunch.

00:07:39.470 --> 00:07:41.030
Yes, yes, I'm sorry.

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:42.670
I didn't recognize you.

00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:44.990
Mr. Benny, may I ask a question?

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:46.200
Want to ask me a question?

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:46.820
Yes, go ahead.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:48.460
Are you part Japanese?

00:07:57.440 --> 00:07:58.220
What'd you say?

00:07:58.800 --> 00:07:59.960
Are you part...

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:12.320
Japanese? Well, I'm about as Japanese as Barry Goldwater. I mean, why do you ask? Well, yesterday

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:17.870
I noticed when bus passengers come in house, must observe Japanese custom of taking shoes

00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:22.520
off. Oh, yes, I do make the customers that come in and take the shoes off. I got that

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:28.960
idea when I was in Tokyo. But why is it some people coming out do not get shoes back?

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:38.540
because some people not pay check.

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:50.280
But, Romy, I'm certainly glad

00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:53.120
that you're enjoying your visit here in America

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:56.700
because I always had such a good time when I was in Tokyo.

00:08:57.020 --> 00:08:59.040
Oh, you're very popular in Tokyo.

00:08:59.280 --> 00:08:59.840
Oh, yeah, my television.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:05.540
shows are there. Yes. Oh, isn't that wonderful. In fact, you're my father's favorite comedian.

00:09:06.590 --> 00:09:11.570
Your father's favorite comedian? Isn't that nice. Your father likes me, huh? Yes, but he's very

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:19.330
worried about you. Your father's worried about me? Yes. He said if you're only 39, you're very

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:29.970
sick man. What are you laughing at?

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:39.260
Well, listen, you thank your father for me,

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:42.160
but tell him that I'm in great shape, not to worry.

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:46.370
And by the way, Romy, I enjoyed your song so much

00:09:46.370 --> 00:09:49.350
that I'd like to have you on my show again, you see.

00:09:49.530 --> 00:09:53.890
Now, how much money would you want to appear regularly on my show?

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:56.630
Well, how much to ask for, I do not know.

00:09:56.950 --> 00:09:58.810
Not very familiar with American money.

00:09:59.320 --> 00:09:59.980
Oh, you're not familiar?

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:01.040
I'm not familiar with American money.

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:08.360
Well, we ought to be able to make a very nice deal then.

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:11.160
For such matters, have agent.

00:10:13.890 --> 00:10:15.090
Oh, you have an agent?

00:10:15.350 --> 00:10:18.290
Yes, and fortunately he accompanied me from Japan,

00:10:18.390 --> 00:10:19.750
and he's backstage now.

00:10:20.030 --> 00:10:21.050
Oh, your agent is backstage?

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:23.570
Well, bring him up. I'd like to talk to him.

00:10:23.570 --> 00:10:23.990
All right.

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:24.670
Okay.

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:28.780
Imagine a Japanese agent.

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:29.960
Oh, I hate to take it.

00:10:30.030 --> 00:10:32.050
of them, but business is business.

00:10:33.950 --> 00:10:37.080
Mr. Benny, would like to introduce honorable agent.

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:39.100
Oh.

00:10:40.270 --> 00:10:45.390
Uh, it is indeed great pleasure to meet young lady's honorable representative.

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:53.670
And this humble person would like to point out that association with Big Star will help her career.

00:10:53.870 --> 00:10:59.900
So financial reward at this time, not important, or how they say it in Japan.

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:03.050
I don't know how they say it in Japan, but just between us.

00:11:03.250 --> 00:11:05.350
Put something in the pot, boy, you ain't got her.

00:11:05.650 --> 00:11:16.210
Put something in the pot?

00:11:16.600 --> 00:11:18.460
Something green, and I don't mean pea pots.

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:22.500
Wait a minute.

00:11:23.140 --> 00:11:24.620
Are you really her agent?

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:26.180
I'm not Barry Goldwater.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:37.320
I cannot understand when you mention agent was under impression that honorable representative

00:11:37.320 --> 00:11:40.200
I'm here to talk business and this guy makes like Charlie Chan

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:47.120
Because I tell him you come back with me from Japan

00:11:47.650 --> 00:11:50.130
Yes, you came back from Tokyo

00:11:50.130 --> 00:11:52.570
I did, I won a two weeks trip on a quiz show

00:11:55.120 --> 00:11:59.020
Look dad, now that we got you out of the twilight zone, let's talk business

00:12:05.340 --> 00:12:12.730
Well, I, uh, I'd like to give her a standard contract, you know, that I give to all of the people that come on my show.

00:12:12.810 --> 00:12:15.610
For instance, it starts out, they get $35 a show.

00:12:16.150 --> 00:12:18.410
$35? I wouldn't let her do a bar mitzvah for that.

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:24.620
$45?

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:27.380
Are you kidding? They pay more in the Peace Corps.

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:34.980
we'll leave stage now it's not nice for women to be around when honorable gentlemen discuss

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:48.440
business keep up pressure i'm sure we can get together on money and i do want romey on my show

00:12:48.440 --> 00:12:57.510
again you see so here i have a contract right here you didn't have to print in japanese that's

00:12:57.510 --> 00:12:59.390
way all my contracts are written.

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:02.070
You know, it works out better than fine print.

00:13:04.480 --> 00:13:07.180
She, you can't afford to miss this opportunity.

00:13:07.780 --> 00:13:10.320
I mean, when she gets to Japan, what chance will she have?

00:13:10.440 --> 00:13:13.500
How many comedians are there in Japan like me?

00:13:13.940 --> 00:13:14.640
Hundreds of them.

00:13:19.030 --> 00:13:20.630
Hundreds of comedians like me?

00:13:21.080 --> 00:13:21.880
One working.

00:13:24.880 --> 00:13:26.820
Look, Mr. Benny, we're not getting any place.

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:29.980
If you're still interested in Miss Yamada, just call this number.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.060
and ask for Jack Sue.

00:13:32.050 --> 00:13:32.870
Jack Sue?

00:13:33.190 --> 00:13:33.750
That's me.

00:13:35.140 --> 00:13:36.540
Hey, wait a minute.

00:13:37.220 --> 00:13:38.820
I, your face is familiar to,

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:41.740
aren't you the fella that's in the picture

00:13:41.740 --> 00:13:45.250
flower drum song you play the part of Sammy Fong?

00:13:45.410 --> 00:13:45.790
That's right.

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:47.350
I thought so.

00:13:47.750 --> 00:13:48.230
Yeah.

00:13:48.990 --> 00:13:56.890
Then why have you been kidding me

00:13:56.890 --> 00:13:58.370
about this agent business?

00:13:58.510 --> 00:13:59.010
I'm not kidding.

00:13:59.110 --> 00:13:59.970
I just got a few sidelines.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:04.750
going for me sidelines yeah want to buy an american transistor

00:14:13.060 --> 00:14:18.060
no i don't but i want to tell you that i also saw you in flower drum song in the

00:14:18.060 --> 00:14:21.340
show in las vegas a great show and you were wonderful thank you very much

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:25.400
but there's one thing i can't understand uh flower drum song is a happy show

00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:29.840
and when i saw you you had tears in your eyes oh well i just

00:14:30.600 --> 00:14:32.240
Came in from the gambling casino.

00:14:32.660 --> 00:14:34.320
I hate to see other people lose.

00:14:35.900 --> 00:14:37.360
And you don't gamble yourself?

00:14:38.320 --> 00:14:39.640
No. No, I don't.

00:14:39.760 --> 00:14:42.420
Well, you're very wise, because a lot of people get hurt in those places.

00:14:43.530 --> 00:14:44.710
Hurt in a gambling casino?

00:14:44.890 --> 00:14:45.610
Let me tell you something.

00:14:45.920 --> 00:14:50.140
The only way I can possibly get hurt in a gambling casino

00:14:50.140 --> 00:14:54.140
is if there's an earthquake and a slot machine falls on my foot.

00:14:55.060 --> 00:14:59.140
I'm in Shursu.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:03.760
I want to thank you very, very much for being on my show.

00:15:04.160 --> 00:15:06.520
And I'm so glad that we met.

00:15:06.940 --> 00:15:08.560
I don't think you realize it, Mr. Benny,

00:15:08.680 --> 00:15:10.500
but actually we met some time ago.

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:11.260
We did?

00:15:11.740 --> 00:15:13.760
Remember, in Japan, about four years ago?

00:15:14.820 --> 00:15:15.740
Oh, yes.

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:17.700
That's the summer that I was in Tokyo.

00:15:18.710 --> 00:15:20.030
Hey, wait a minute.

00:15:21.080 --> 00:15:23.520
Don't tell me you're one of the guys that picketed me

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:25.180
because I was diving for pearls.

00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:28.740
It was at the Ginza Theater.

00:15:29.480 --> 00:15:29.960
At the Ginza Theater?

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:31.660
I was in M.C. Young.

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:33.680
You did a Ned Sullivan show in Tokyo.

00:15:33.860 --> 00:15:35.480
I was in the audience. That's right.

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:37.880
I remember that. You should remember.

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:39.120
I'll never forget it.

00:15:39.320 --> 00:15:41.920
I remember that particular Sunday

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:43.880
we started the show as usual.

00:15:44.530 --> 00:15:57.060
Ed Surabachi Show.

00:16:02.590 --> 00:16:05.820
Good evening, ladies and gentlemen, and welcome to our shoot.

00:16:07.740 --> 00:16:09.820
Tonight we have a really big show.

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:15.800
Especially for the children, we have Sumoto Takamira giving karate lessons.

00:16:16.980 --> 00:16:21.120
So parents, the next time you argue with your children, watch your throat.

00:16:21.760 --> 00:16:28.460
For a really big finish.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:33.060
Right here on our stage, Mount Fujiyama will erupt.

00:16:35.040 --> 00:16:35.940
Right here.

00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:39.320
So watch the molten lava in living color.

00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:44.850
As we get on with the show,

00:16:45.150 --> 00:16:48.660
we present the finalists of our talent contest.

00:16:49.560 --> 00:16:51.940
The winner receives 10,000 yen.

00:16:52.880 --> 00:16:54.380
10,000 yen?

00:16:55.040 --> 00:16:55.320
On with the show.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.940
So let's see who wins all that money.

00:17:02.520 --> 00:17:05.920
Our first contestants, the Hooraki fellows.

00:17:06.460 --> 00:17:06.980
Let's have it.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:02.440
Thank you so much, ladies and gentlemen. I hope you enjoyed the show.

00:20:03.160 --> 00:20:09.180
And I want to thank Miss Yamari and Mr. Su for appearing on this program.

00:20:09.700 --> 00:20:12.550
And come out of here again, will you, kids? Come on.

00:20:20.300 --> 00:20:25.510
Mr. Benny, is that story true that you're being in a contest in Japan?

00:20:26.100 --> 00:20:29.580
Yes, yes, that's true. And we didn't win.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:39.500
Of course, we didn't win the contest, and I felt pretty bad about it until I found out that 10,000 yen was only $16.

00:20:40.280 --> 00:20:43.080
No, no, Mr. Benny. 10,000 yen is $28.

00:20:44.110 --> 00:20:47.340
Oh. Oh, well, now I feel bad again.

00:20:50.380 --> 00:20:52.620
Thanks so much for being on the show.

00:20:53.080 --> 00:20:54.100
Thank you, Mr. Benny.

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:59.980
But I'm disappointed that you and Mr. Su could not agree on price for me, so I could...

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:01.720
we go on another show for you.

00:21:02.050 --> 00:21:03.790
This make me feel very bad.

00:21:04.010 --> 00:21:06.150
Oh, well, listen, listen, honey.

00:21:06.310 --> 00:21:07.390
This was all a gag.

00:21:07.870 --> 00:21:10.030
We were just playing a part, that's all.

00:21:10.210 --> 00:21:12.090
You're going to be on my show again.

00:21:12.450 --> 00:21:14.030
That make me very happy.

00:21:14.430 --> 00:21:17.090
And you know what, I thought of a wonderful idea.

00:21:17.310 --> 00:21:19.190
You see, the next time when you sing a song,

00:21:19.410 --> 00:21:22.650
then I'll accompany you on my violin, you see?

00:21:22.990 --> 00:21:23.730
Your violin.

00:21:23.950 --> 00:21:26.080
Now you make me feel bad again.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:32.080
Well, we'll discuss this later.

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:33.160
Goodbye.

00:21:33.540 --> 00:21:34.300
Thank you.

00:21:34.620 --> 00:21:34.920
So long.

00:21:35.320 --> 00:21:35.640
So long.

00:21:42.360 --> 00:21:44.500
Well, good night, folks, and I'll be seeing you soon.

00:22:01.370 --> 00:22:06.550
Here at Comedy Central, we've got That Girl, starring Marlo Thomas as Anne-Marie,

00:22:06.850 --> 00:22:11.290
a young actress trying to make him the big city without sleeping her way to the top.
